<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Menu style Classic+'s option screens (1.1.3, the owner's Classic+ plan part B): SETTINGS' CONTROLS, GRAPHICS,
     SOUND, INTERFACE, ONLINE and ADVANCED, each the settings panel's player-facing rows of that kind in the look of the
     Xbox's own ADVANCED CONTROLS (classic/xbox_screens.xml: ui.map's gradient, the heading at 29,11 - made of the
     game's letters, menu_titles.c, else the port's drawn one: tools/classic_menu_art.py -, rows of option_bkds
     512 x 28 at 54,73 and 30 apart, the label in large_ui at the left, the value between arrow_sm_left and
     arrow_sm_right at the right, the focused row's help in white large_ui under them, the button key at the foot).
     Eight rows a screen, the rest scrolled to as GAME MANAGER's are; a row without a value opens its page on the same
     screen - the parent's heading kept, the page's name on the line under it, the rows a line lower - and Circle goes
     back up. A change applies at once, as the panel's (no CANCEL/ACCEPT). Which rows: port/linux/game/
     classic_options.h; their words, values and help: the panel's own (settings_rows.h); menu_functions.c ce_opt_*.
     An action asks first in the Xbox's question (semi_transparent_grey, alert_bkd: as QUIT does). -->
<menus>
	<strings name="ce/opt_text">
		<string text="%a-button =OK   %b-button =CANCEL"/>
	</strings>
